The deeper you go, the warmer it gets. You're sweating. For a second you re-
gret that you ever agreed to help the Temple in their problems with the Apos-
tolate. Sure, you're a personal friend of the Prior and the Abbess, but who
are you to solve ALL their problems? Why are you the only one who cares about
all the big things? First the Book of Stars, now the Apostolate, and in addi-
tion the minor requests by other people. Your grandfather once told you that
being able to reject people's demands is important, but somehow you can't.

"Anyway", you mumble. You agreed, so you're here and you won't fail. You look
around. "Walls. Floors. Just more of the same." You sigh. Somehow you can un-
derstand people who want to go back to the surface. Even the Abbess is trying.
Suddenly you hear steps in the distance. Steps...and voices? Yes, clearly
there are people talking. Other travellers? Then you see men, women, even
some children, clothed in black linen, speaking quietly. Their clothes are
similar to the style of the old woman you met in the Forgotten Realm.

"It seems I've found them", you whisper. But how to approach them? They seem
already alert and distrustful. You think for some minutes and then decide not
to hide, but to officially join their cult. Only when you look weaker than you
are, and seeking for guidance by them, they would trust you. You exhale and,
while trying to look unsure and nervous, approach one of the novices.
